{"schemaVersion":1,"workId":"OL53994W","title":"The Prince and the Pauper","authors":["Mark Twain"],"firstPublished":1881,"edition":{"description":"Sections as detected in Project Gutenberg eBook #1837.","source":"Project Gutenberg eBook #1837","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1837"},"sectionLabel":{"singular":"Chapter","plural":"Chapters"},"sections":[{"id":"s1","label":"Ch. 1","title":"The birth of the Prince and the Pauper."},{"id":"s2","label":"Ch. 2","title":"Tom’s early life."},{"id":"s3","label":"Ch. 3","title":"Tom’s meeting with the Prince."},{"id":"s4","label":"Ch. 4","title":"The Prince’s troubles begin."},{"id":"s5","label":"Ch. 5","title":"Tom as a Patrician."},{"id":"s6","label":"Ch. 6","title":"Tom receives instructions."},{"id":"s7","label":"Ch. 7","title":"Tom’s first royal dinner."},{"id":"s8","label":"Ch. 8","title":"The Question of the Seal."},{"id":"s9","label":"Ch. 9","title":"The river pageant."},{"id":"s10","label":"Ch. 10","title":"The Prince in the toils."},{"id":"s11","label":"Ch. 11","title":"At Guildhall."},{"id":"s12","label":"Ch. 12","title":"The Prince and his Deliverer."},{"id":"s13","label":"Ch. 13","title":"The disappearance of the Prince."},{"id":"s14","label":"Ch. 14","title":"‘Le Roi est mort--vive le Roi.’"},{"id":"s15","label":"Ch. 15","title":"Tom as King."},{"id":"s16","label":"Ch. 16","title":"The State Dinner."},{"id":"s17","label":"Ch. 17","title":"Foo-foo the First."},{"id":"s18","label":"Ch. 18","title":"The Prince with the Tramps."},{"id":"s19","label":"Ch. 19","title":"The Prince with the peasants."},{"id":"s20","label":"Ch. 20","title":"The Prince and the hermit."},{"id":"s21","label":"Ch. 21","title":"Hendon to the rescue."},{"id":"s22","label":"Ch. 22","title":"A Victim of Treachery."},{"id":"s23","label":"Ch. 23","title":"The Prince a prisoner."},{"id":"s24","label":"Ch. 24","title":"The Escape."},{"id":"s25","label":"Ch. 25","title":"Hendon Hall."},{"id":"s26","label":"Ch. 26","title":"Disowned."},{"id":"s27","label":"Ch. 27","title":"In Prison."},{"id":"s28","label":"Ch. 28","title":"The sacrifice."},{"id":"s29","label":"Ch. 29","title":"To London."},{"id":"s30","label":"Ch. 30","title":"Tom’s progress."},{"id":"s31","label":"Ch. 31","title":"The Recognition procession."},{"id":"s32","label":"Ch. 32","title":"Coronation Day."},{"id":"s33","label":"Ch. 33","title":"Edward as King."}],"groups":[{"id":"g-canty","label":"Canty (shared surname)"},{"id":"g-hendon","label":"Hendon (shared surname)"}],"characters":[{"id":"king","name":"King","role":"protagonist","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “Among, but not of, the dreadful rabble that inhabited the house, was a good old priest whom the King had turned out of house and home with a pension of a few farthings, and he used to get the children aside and teach…”"},{"id":"tom-canty","name":"Tom Canty","aliases":["Tom"],"role":"protagonist","group":"g-canty","firstAppearance":"s1","summary":"First mention: “But there was no talk about the other baby, Tom Canty, lapped in his poor rags, except among the family of paupers whom he had just come to trouble with his presence.”"},{"id":"miles-hendon","name":"Miles Hendon","aliases":["Hendon","Miles"],"role":"protagonist","group":"g-hendon","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “Here stand I by thy side to prove it; and mind I tell thee thou might’st have a worser friend than Miles Hendon and yet not tire thy legs with seeking.”"},{"id":"lord-hertford","name":"Hertford","aliases":["Lord Hertford"],"role":"supporting","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Take instant order for it, my lord Hertford.””"},{"id":"john-canty","name":"John Canty","aliases":["St. John"],"role":"supporting","group":"g-canty","firstAppearance":"s2","summary":"First mention: “They got drunk whenever they could; then they fought each other or anybody else who came in the way; they cursed and swore always, drunk or sober; John Canty was a thief, and his mother a beggar.”"},