:"minor","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: “If my father liveth still, after these seven years that I have heard nought from home in my foreign dungeon, he will welcome the poor lad and give him generous shelter for my sake; so will my good elder brother, Arthu…”"},{"id":"humphrey","name":"Humphrey","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s14","summary":"First mention: “I am Humphrey--Humphrey Marlow.””"},{"id":"lord-protector","name":"Lord Protector","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s15","summary":"First mention: “There were greater matters in the programme--for on that day he would have to preside at a council which would take his views and commands concerning the policy to be pursued toward various foreign nations scattered f…”"},{"id":"sir-richard","name":"Sir Richard","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: “My father, Sir Richard, is very rich, and of a most generous nature.”"},{"id":"lord-mayor","name":"Lord Mayor","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s6","summary":"First mention: “When it came out that the little ladies were to accompany him to the Lord Mayor’s banquet in the evening, his heart gave a bound of relief and delight, for he felt that he should not be friendless, now, among that mul…”"},{"id":"kent","name":"Kent","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s12","summary":"First mention: “My father is a baronet--one of the smaller lords by knight service {2}--Sir Richard Hendon of Hendon Hall, by Monk’s Holm in Kent.””"},{"id":"lady-jane-grey","name":"Lady Jane Grey","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s3","summary":"First mention: ““The Lady Elizabeth, my sister, is fourteen, and the Lady Jane Grey, my cousin, is of mine own age, and comely and gracious withal; but my sister the Lady Mary, with her gloomy mien and--Look you: do thy sisters forbi…”"},{"id":"chancellor","name":"Chancellor","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “The Lord Chancellor entered, and knelt by the King’s couch, saying--”"},{"i